OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F402A1786967345
OL,3,CFamily pay tribute to artist who died
OL,4,Cfollowing Shaldon collision
OL,6,F69-year-old Elizabeth Brown, from
OL,7,FTaunton in Somerset, passed away at
OL,8,Fthe scene.
OL,10,FHer family have paid tribute,
OL,11,Fdescribing her as a "dear friend to
OL,12,Fmany".
OL,14,FThey said: "Liz leaves behind her
OL,15,Fchildren Camilla and Alastair, her
OL,16,Fpartner Simon and her brother Andrew.
OL,17,FLast year, Liz became a proud
OL,18,Fgrandmother to Circe.
OL,26,@sD@UOUtD@EO]vD@LOU
OL,1,W~s1j5 hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}      G2/4
OL,2,W,.!+.-' "-$/*%+.!+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BSW Eng NewsCThis Day FReg TV
FL,403,400,120,260,000,100
PN,40203
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F402A1786967345
OL,3,CFamily pay tribute to artist who died
OL,4,Cfollowing Shaldon collision
OL,6,F"Liz was an artist. She loved colour
OL,7,Fand created big bright paintings that
OL,8,Freflect her personality: strong,
OL,9,Fbright, intuitive, and warm.
OL,11,F"She had a beautiful final day,
OL,12,Fspending time with Simon and her
OL,13,Fcockapoo Bertie, swimming at Ness
OL,14,FBeach in the sunshine.
OL,16,F"We would like to thank everyone that
OL,17,Fhas sent kind messages of support
OL,18,Fduring the difficult weeks following.
OL,19,FWe will continue to remember her for
OL,20,Fthe amazing woman she was every day."
OL,26,@nD@AOUsD@AOUxD@AOU|D@eO]
